  "exception": {
    "type": "no-defensible-ucr-match",
    "checkedOn": "2026-11-09",
    "reason": "The Arabic language and culture direction needs sustained Arabic instruction and work with Arabic sources. The regional culture and politics directions also lack a course sequence centred on the Middle East and North Africa. UCR offers substantive comparative work on Arabic myths, the Islamic eastern Mediterranean, empires and conflict. These contributions are distributed across courses with wider or different academic centres, and do not provide enough regional or Arabic-language depth for a programme-level comparison.",
    "curriculumContext": "The Arabic Studies major includes a common first year, a required Cairo semester in the second year, and a thesis using Arabic sources. The 30 EC free-choice space is separate from the Cairo semester. The writing diagnostic and study tutoring carry no credits.",
    "ucrCourseEvidence": "Reviewed all 151 current courses for Arabic language, literature, media, Islamic and Middle Eastern history, and region-centred society and politics. World Myth & Literature includes Arabic and Near Eastern materials in comparative narrative study. Renaissance Italy & Global Mediterranean considers Islamic courts and trans-Mediterranean exchanges in a course centred on Renaissance art. History of Empires includes ancient Persia in a worldwide comparison. Psycholinguistics develops methods for studying acquisition and bilingualism. Style & Meaning, Life & Travel Writing and Perspectives on Literary Meaning develop methods for analysing form, identity and texts. Modern History, sociology, qualitative methods and heritage offer context and methods. Comparative Politics, International Relations, Peace & Conflict and international law support comparative analysis of institutions and conflict. Taken together these courses supply real points of connection, but no Arabic proficiency progression or sustained sequence in Arab and Middle Eastern societies, politics, history or sources. No scheduling limitation determines the result.",
    "candidateAssessment": [
      {
        "concept": "Arabic language, literature and source-based cultural study",
        "generatingRegistryRows": [
          16669,
          16670,
          16671,
